cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use astro-duck in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "astro-duck: A DuckDB extension for astronomical calculations"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Björn
    family-names: Bethge
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4500-0274"
repository-code: "https://github.com/synapticore-io/astro-duck"
url: "https://github.com/synapticore-io/astro-duck"
license: MIT
version: "1.4.0"
date-released: "2026-04-17"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.19482715"
    description: "Concept DOI - resolves to the latest version"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.19645339"
    description: "DOI for version 1.4.0"
abstract: >-
  astro-duck is a DuckDB extension that brings 62 functions (59 scalar
  + 3 FITS table functions) to SQL: coordinate
  transforms (RA/Dec to Cartesian, ICRS to galactic frames), angular
  separation on the celestial sphere, photometric conversions
  (magnitude/flux, distance modulus, absolute magnitude), CCM89 +
  O'Donnell 1994 dust extinction with standard UBVRIJHK photometric
  bands, cosmological distances (luminosity, comoving), celestial body
  models (main-sequence stars, white dwarfs, neutron stars, black
  holes, brown dwarfs, rocky planets, gas giants, ice giants,
  asteroids), Keplerian orbital mechanics, 3D octree spatial indexing,
  Newtonian gravitational dynamics, sidereal time / observation
  planning (GMST, LMST, hour angle, equatorial to horizontal alt/az
  conversion, Julian Date from TIMESTAMP/TIMESTAMPTZ), and FITS file
  I/O (fits_hdus, fits_header, read_fits via cfitsio). It is designed
  for vectorized batch processing of astronomical catalogs (Gaia DR3,
  SDSS, NASA Exoplanet Archive, simulation snapshots, FITS archives)
  directly in a single DuckDB process.
keywords:
